# Token-economy rules for a fixed per-engineer budget. Copy to the root of any repo.

## Working style
- Read only the files you need. Use search (grep/glob) before opening large files, and read
  ranges instead of whole files when a file is over 300 lines.
- Do not re-read a file you already have in context unless it changed.
- Keep replies short: what you changed, why, and what to verify. No restating the request.
- Prefer targeted edits (search/replace) over rewriting whole files.
- Batch independent tool calls in one turn.

## Context hygiene
- When a task spans many files, summarize what you have learned so far in one paragraph
  before moving on, so context can be compacted without losing state.
- Do not paste large command output back into the conversation; tail or grep it.
- Do not run the browser tool unless the task is UI verification.

## Knowledge base
- Before asking the user about team conventions, service names, or deploy steps, call
  `search_knowledge_base` and cite the source URI.

## Safety
- Never print secrets, tokens, account ids, or credentials into the conversation.
- Ask before running destructive git or infrastructure commands.
